.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1038/nprot.2015.121</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC4689599</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">26513671</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Estes MK, Ettayebi K, Tenge VR, Murakami K, Karandikar U, Lin SC, Ayyar BV, Cortes-Penfield NW, Haga K, Neill FH, Opekun AR, Broughman JR, Zeng XL, Blutt SE, Crawford SE, Ramani S, Graham DY, Atmar RL. 2019. Human norovirus cultivation in nontransformed stem cell-derived human intestinal enteroid cultures: success and challenges. Viruses 11:638. 10.3390/v11070638.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.3390/v11070638</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC6669637</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">31336765</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Baldridge MT, Turula H, Wobus CE. 2016. Norovirus regulation by host and microbe. Trends Mol Med 22:1047&#8211;1059. 10.1016/j.molmed.2016.10.003.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1016/j.molmed.2016.10.003</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC5135607</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">27887808</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Wobus CE, Karst SM, Thackray LB, Chang KO, Sosnovtsev SV, Belliot G, Krug A, Mackenzie JM, Green KY, Virgin HW. 2004. Replication of norovirus in cell culture reveals a tropism for dendritic cells and macrophages. PLoS Biol 2:e432. 10.1371/journal.pbio.0020432.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1371/journal.pbio.0020432</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC532393</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">15562321</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Karst SM, Wobus CE, Lay M, Davidson J, Virgin HW. 2003. STAT1-dependent innate immunity to a Norwalk-like virus. Science 299:1575&#8211;1578. 10.1126/science.1077905.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1126/science.1077905</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">12624267</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></